+- `"ephemeral"`: one-shot `completeSimple` requests (including titles and prompted judges), side turns, advisors, cache warming, and auto-learn capture. These requests have no primary pending-turn resume contract. `sessionId` and `parentSessionId` still serve transport/cache affinity and are not proof of primary ownership.
+- Missing/unknown provenance: fail closed in providers requiring durable primary admission. Bare `streamSimple` calls are not automatically labeled ephemeral. No session-ID prefix or model/provider-name heuristics are used.
+
+`completeSimple` defaults to `"ephemeral"` but preserves an explicit `"primary"` override. Primary `AgentSession` dispatch always stamps `"primary"` and the current provider ID; side wrappers overwrite inherited provenance with `"ephemeral"`. The native gateway serializer strips `requestKind`; it is a local host ownership claim, not an authorization field accepted from the wire. Revalidate live IDs after `/fresh` and reset rather than caching a transcript-ID mapping forever.
+
+`BRIDGE_ADMISSION_PAUSED`, `BRIDGE_ADMISSION_STOPPED`, and execution-unknown outcomes veto automatic recovery, fallback, compaction, stop-hook continuation, and queued-message draining. Paused is a resumable, proven-unsent outcome, not `execution_unknown`; stopped requires setup repair. Throwing a custom provider error with string `code`/`type` and numeric `status` retains those fields on the assistant failure.
